<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kinai</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Kinki region</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kinai, 'the home provinces', was the region around the old Japanese capitals of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nara">Nara</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyoto">Kyoto</a>, made up of the five provinces of Yamashiro, Yamato, Kawachi, Izumi and Settsu. As the land of the imperial court and later of the Ashikaga <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shogun">shoguns</a>, it was the political and economic centre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, and control of it was the goal of the warlords of the 16th century. Roughly the same area forms today's Kansai.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kinai.jpg" alt="Kinai" width="320" height="326" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 百楽兎 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kinai.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
